<h1>Round up</h1>
<h2>September 12, 2026</h2>
I discuss various topics today.
<a name="2026-09-12-september-11"> </a>
<h3>September 11</h3>
<p>I have discussed September 11 <a href="blog:20120911">multiple</a>  
times <a href="blog:2019-09-12">previously</a>. 
This time, on the 25<sup style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 0; vertical-align: 5px">th</sup>
 anniversary of the attacks, I ended up being only one block away from
 where I was when I saw the north tower collapse live on TV because my
 girlfriend asked me to visit her there.
<a name="2026-09-12-nikita-tyukalos-parties"> </a>
<h3>Nikita Tyukalo’s parties</h3>
<p>It would seem that <a href="AI-summaries/2026-08-29-PartyHouse.html">Nikita Tyukalo had extensive loud  parties</a>, 
parties which were
 apparently funded by him trafficking women to be online pornographic
 models.
<a name="2026-09-12-andrew-tate-denied-bail"> </a>
<h3>Andrew Tate: Denied bail</h3>
<p>Andrew Tate and his brother have been <a href="AI-summaries/2026-09-09-TatesNoBail.html">denied bail</a> 
in their extradition proceedings. They remain in jail.
<p>Tate has allegedly <a href="AI-summaries/2026-08-28-webcam.html">trafficked webcam models to earn money</a>, 
among other charges.
<a name="2026-09-12-nathan-cofnas-update"> </a>
<h3>Nathan Cofnas update</h3>
<p>Nathan Cofnas, who accused a Black professor of plagiarism, has had
 his <a href="AI-summaries/2026-08-30-CofnasUpdate.html">suspension ended</a>, 
but is not allowed to teach classes. It would seem
 they don’t want to fire him—but I very seriously doubt they will renew
 his contract either.
<p>Nathan Cofnas has a right to be a “race realist” who believes, to put
 it bluntly, that <a href="AI-summaries/2026-08-26-brussels.html">Black people aren’t as smart</a> 
as other races. I strongly disagree
 with that belief, but he has a right to have it. Where he crossed the
 line was digging up dirt to <a href="AI-summaries/2026-08-26-bbc.html">harass someone for being  Black</a>.
<a name="2026-09-12-woke-1-was-crazy"> </a>
<h3>Woke 1 was crazy</h3>
<p>The same left-leaning media who were part of the “Woke 1” movement
 are now realizing how out of touch that movement was.
<p>The New York times, who <a href="blog:2020-06-08">forced an editor to  resign</a> 
back in 2020—peak Woke—for publishing
 the opinion of a US Senator, recently published an <a href="AI-summaries/2027-09-10-Woke.html">article about how crazy “Woke 1” really was</a>. 
How times have changed.
<a name="2026-09-12-lowering-memory-prices"> </a>
<h3>Lowering memory prices</h3>
<p>One startup is working on a <a href="AI-summaries/2027-09-12-CheapMemory.html">much cheaper process to create computer memory</a>. 
This process will
 hopefully make memory cheaper by the end of the decade. I personally
 feel the AI bubble will burst before then.
<p>Either way, it should be possible to get a ThinkPad T14s with an
 Intel i7 processor, 64 gigs of memory, and 4tb or more of hard disk
 space for under $2000 within three years.


